 "findings": [
  "For the 25 careful students, the check put English within 0.15 of the truth for 88% of them, against 64% if we just assumed every student was average for the class.",
  "It found on average 2.48 of the same 5 simulated students that their true traits would pick (assuming average gets 1.72).",
  "Its advice was within 0.35 marks out of 10 of the advice we'd give if we knew the student perfectly, and it picked the same best tool for 100% of them (assuming average: 0.55 marks, 100%).",
  "The weakest part is learning speed: off by 0.128 on average, against 0.105 for assuming average. It comes from the change between two 5-question quizzes, so one lucky guess moves it a lot.",
  "The didn't-try flag caught 7 of the 7 students who clicked through or quit, flagged 0 of 8 who rushed, and wrongly flagged 0 of 25 careful students."
